      },
      "message": "fix(mcp): locate_part takes mate ids by the one pick rule\n\nThe audit of #692 after #705/#709 found one picker left outside the\nrule: MCP locate_part parsed its mate ids without pick::check_pickable,\nso a vertex along a round rim or inside a face became a mate point. It\nnow runs the same check as every other MCP pick. The user guide gets a\n\"What a click picks\" section; centre picks wait for #759.\n\nPinned by mcp_pick::locate_part_refuses_a_mate_point_no_click_could_pick.\n\nRefs #692\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
